  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USAID Youth-Powered Ecosystem to Advance Urban Adolescent Health and Well-Being (YPE4AH)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Nigeria):  With FY 2022 funds this activity will:.Strengthen adolescent access to youth-friendly RH/FP and nutrition services;.Ensure the Youth Hubs and surrounding facilities continue to be operated as safe spaces for adolescents; .Provide training, internship and apprenticeship opportunities for adolescents by leveraging private sector support and opportunities; and.Build the capacity of three local partners to increasingly play an important role in the management cycle of USAID and other partners&apos; development efforts, furthering USAID&apos;s localization efforts..Youth Powered Ecosystem to Advance Urban Adolescent Health (YPE4AH) is a five-year cooperative agreement designed through a co-creation process to empower young Nigerians to access the skills, social capital, and resources needed to realize their futures. This activity will improve the health and well-being of urban, underprivileged, out-of-school, and unmarried adolescents (especially girls) aged 15-19  by increasing voluntary family planning (FP) uptake and continued use. The activity focuses on designated Youth Hubs which are safe spaces for youth to seek and access FP and reproductive health (RH) information and referrals in urban slums, in four Local Government Areas (LGAs) in Kano and Lagos States. These are the two largest urban areas in the country and reflect diverse cultural and socioeconomic contexts, providing an opportunity to inform adaptation to different zones and scale-up for greater impact. The activity has adapted and is scaling up evidence-based, high-impact SKILLZ curricula (a skills-building program), which combines sports, fun-based activities and group sessions led by youth coaches, age 20-28, to spur healthy behavior change and to shift attitudes towards more equitable gender norms. .This activity contributes directly to USAID Nigeria CDCS Development Objective 2, the Embassy&apos;s ICS, and is closely aligned with Goal 3 of the Joint Strategic Plan...</narrative>
  </description>
